commit 4937a8ea061f6779cde5faf1cf7c4d184a641a4f
Author: aldiss <v.drobkov@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 31 21:36:56 2026 +0200

    dashboard: render a prompt bus-timeout as "No response", not "Answered in terminal" (dl-13559)
    
    The real-DOM arm2 caught a client lifecycle defect: a PromptBus timeout
    (prompt_cancel) was rendered to the operator as "Answered in terminal" — a false
    claim that the prompt was answered in the TUI. Chain: useMessageHandler's
    prompt_cancel case called dismissInteractiveRequest → status "dismissed" → every
    renderer maps "dismissed" to "Answered in terminal". The enum already had a
    distinct "cancelled" status the path ignored.
    
    Fix (client-state truthfulness; TUI dismiss semantics untouched):
    - event-reducer.ts: add cancelInteractiveRequest — a sister of
      dismissInteractiveRequest, identical except it sets status "cancelled" on the
      request and the message args. Pending-only. Exported.
    - useMessageHandler.ts: route case "prompt_cancel" (a bus timeout — nobody
      answered) to cancelInteractiveRequest. Leave case "prompt_dismiss" (a genuine
      TUI answer) on dismissInteractiveRequest, and ui_dismiss unchanged.
    - All six interactive renderers: status "cancelled" now renders "No response"
      (was "Cancelled"; Generic gained the case). "dismissed" still renders
      "Answered in terminal".
    - prompt-bus.ts: correct remaining ANSWER-only comments to the RESPONDER
      semantic (author = answerer OR authenticated dismisser; renderedBy separate).
      Comments only, no logic change.
    
    RED→GREEN: reducer (cancel sets "cancelled", no-op unless pending), handler
    (prompt_cancel → "cancelled", prompt_dismiss → "dismissed" preserved), renderers
    (cancelled → "No response" and NOT "Answered in terminal"; dismissed preserved).
    Updates the two pre-existing renderer tests that pinned the old "Cancelled" label.

